Package: cellspecR
Title: Read, Validate and Store Multiplexed Imaging Cell Tables
Version: 1.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("R.", "Heller",
           email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Defines 'cellspec', a versioned table format for segmented
    cells from multiplexed tissue images: cell identifiers, centroids in
    micrometres, per-marker measurements with an explicit compartment and
    statistic, image and channel metadata, and provenance. Reads
    measurement exports of image-analysis tools such as 'QuPath' and
    'MCMICRO' into this format, validates its structure and content,
    selects one signal per marker through an explicit policy, and writes
    directories with a 'SHA-256' checksum manifest so that later analysis
    steps can verify what they read. 'QuPath' is described by Bankhead et
    al. (2017) <doi:10.1038/s41598-017-17204-5> and 'MCMICRO' by Schapiro
    et al. (2022) <doi:10.1038/s41592-021-01308-y>.
